#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
luksury - TPM2-backed automatic unlocking for classic systemd-boot LUKS2 roots.

This tool does not implement TPM sealing or LUKS unlocking itself.  It wires up
the systemd components that do:

  * systemd-cryptenroll  - enrolls a TPM2 token into the LUKS2 header
  * systemd-pcrlock      - builds a TPM NV policy from the measured boot
  * systemd-cryptsetup   - unseals the key at boot

It is intentionally aimed at the classic "vmlinuz + initrd" systemd-boot
layout, not at unified kernel images (UKIs).  The update hook refreshes the
pcrlock policy after a kernel/initrd update; the LUKS token itself does not
need to be re-enrolled.

Commands:
  luksury setup [--mode=auto|pcrlock|literal]
  luksury update [--initrd PATH] [--cmdline PATH] [--kernel VERSION]
  luksury status
  luksury remove

Run `luksury <command> --help` for the options of each command.
"""

